# Normalise line endings for text files in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# lib/toast.ps1 and lib/focus.ps1 are Windows PowerShell 5.1 scripts and must
# keep their EXACT bytes: toast.ps1 is deliberately pure ASCII + UTF-8 BOM.
#
# Why this matters (a real bug this project already hit): PowerShell 5.1 decodes
# .ps1 files using the ANSI code page unless a UTF-8 BOM is present. Without the
# BOM, a multi-byte sequence in a comment swallowed the following newline, so the
# line after it was folded into the comment -- the script still *parsed*, it just
# silently stopped setting activationType="protocol" on the toast, and
# click-to-focus died while every other check stayed green.
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending and encoding conversion, so a fresh clone gets
# byte-identical scripts no matter how core.autocrlf is configured locally.
*.ps1 -text
